          "message": "build(wasm): reach cargo check green for wasm32 core (Phase 2 — vector + persistence gating) (#3776)\n\n## Summary\n\nBuilds on the merged Phase-1 foundation (#3772), which crossed the\ndependency\nlayer by gating the wasm-hostile crates behind `cfg(not(target_arch =\n\"wasm32\"))`.\nThis wave gates the remaining **source-level use-sites** of the two\nexternal\nsubsystems that cannot compile to `wasm32-unknown-unknown` — the\n`usearch`\nvector index and the `redb`/persistence I/O tier — out of the wasm\nprofile, so\n`cargo check --target wasm32-unknown-unknown --no-default-features` now\npasses\nfor the core graph + temporal + query surface.\n\nNative is unchanged: both `cargo check` (default) and `cargo check\n--no-default-features` still pass. This is a **compile-check** milestone\n—\nruntime functionality on wasm (in-memory fs/thread, a JS clock) is Phase\n3.\n\n## What changed\n\n**Fork A — vector index (usearch)**\n- Gates the `usearch`-backed `HnswIndex` plus the sharded/distributed\nvector\n  submodules out on wasm behind an inert `NotImplemented` stub, keeping\n`HnswConfig`/`DistanceMetric` compiling; serial fallback for the\ntemporal\n  snapshot scan.\n\n**Fork B — redb / index-persistence**\n- `storage/index_persistence`: the pure types (`PersistenceConfig`,\n`PersistenceTracker`, `IndexPersistenceManager`, the CRC/`common`\nhelpers,\n`formats`, `manifest`, `strings`, `temporal`, `temporal_adjacency`) stay\ncompiled on **all** targets; only the `memmap2`/`zstd`/`rayon`/`usearch`\nsubmodules (`operations`, `vector`, `worker`, `reencrypt`) and `graph`'s\nzstd/memmap I/O functions are gated out. `graph`'s pure property-map\nhelpers\n  (used by the temporal index) stay always-compiled.\n- `db`: the crash-safe `write_durable` primitive is extracted into a new\nalways-compiled `db::durable_write` module so the encryption-state\nauthority\n  keeps it on wasm; the redb/encryption engines (`rotation`,\n  `encryption_enable`, `encryption_disable`) and `AletheiaDB::open` /\n`open_from_env` are gated out on wasm (`AletheiaDB::new` stays). The\ndurable\nbranch of `with_unified_config`\n(resume/rotation/cold-storage/index-load) is\ngated so wasm compiles only the ephemeral in-memory path;\n`persist_indexes`\n  is an inert no-op on wasm.\n- `stats` / `temporal`: hot-only cold-tier fallbacks on wasm.\n- `bin/aletheia`: the OS-facing CLI\n(daemon/subprocess/backup/restore/rotation)\nis compiled out on wasm behind `mod native_cli`, leaving an inert entry\npoint.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `cargo check --target wasm32-unknown-unknown --no-default-features` —\n**green** (0 errors)\n- `cargo check` (default) — green\n- `cargo check --no-default-features` — green\n\n## Out of scope (Phase 3)\n\nRuntime wasm functionality: in-memory filesystem/thread shims and a\nJS-backed\nclock. `std::fs`/`std::thread`/`std::time` compile on wasm today (they\nonly\nfail/panic at runtime), so they are intentionally not gated here.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_01MoamPP7bAkAb7hcvBmS6ps)_\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>",
